## 2. Real Dev Examples (read aloud once each — match the rhythm)

### Example 1 — Login bug (Template A — S-R-F-I)

> **Symptom:** Users got logged out right after signing in — felt like the login screen was a loop.
> **Root cause:** I tracked it down to SecureStore — we saved the token, **but** we didn't set the auth state to `authenticated` in the same call, so the navigator redirected to Login before the state updated.
> **Fix:** I moved the state update right after `saveTokens`, before returning from the login action.
> **Impact:** Every user on the latest build. Rolled out as a hotfix this morning — error rate dropped to zero in 10 minutes.

### Example 2 — Race condition (Template A — with hedging)

> **Symptom:** The feed list flickered — sometimes showed old data for a second, then updated.
> **Root cause:** **I'm not 100% sure yet — my best guess is** a race between the cached query and the refetch. **For example,** when the user goes from profile back to feed, both the cache and the new request update the state at almost the same time.
> **Fix:** Still investigating. **In the meantime,** I added a loading flag to hide the list during refetch — it's a patch, not the real fix.
> **Impact:** Cosmetic on iOS, not critical. No users reported it yet — I caught it in QA.

### Example 3 — Performance bug (Template B — R-I-F)

> **Repro:** Open the feed, scroll 20 items, memory jumps 150MB on iOS.
> **Investigation:** I profiled with React DevTools. **First,** I suspected the image list — ruled out. **Then,** I checked the item component — it re-rendered on every scroll **because** the `onPress` handler was recreated inline. **In other words,** every scroll frame was rebuilding the whole list.
> **Fix:** Wrapped the handler in `useCallback` with a stable dep. Memory is flat now, scroll is smooth.
> **Impact:** Affected mid-range Android devices most — a few users reported lag in the last release. Regression test added.

